  "question": {
    "text": "When a missile is fired from a ship, the probability that it is intercepted is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and the probability that the missile hits the target, given that it is not intercepted, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> If three missiles are fired independently from the ship, then the probability that all three hit the target, is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>",
